    <briefdescription>
<para>RAID/Merkle proof of artifact integrity in a batch tree. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Supports O(log N) membership proof: given <computeroutput>leaf_hash</computeroutput> and the <computeroutput>proof_path</computeroutput> sibling hashes, a verifier can recompute the Merkle root and compare with the authoritative <computeroutput>merkle_root</computeroutput>.</para>
<para>Proof path format: each element is a pair { &quot;hash&quot;: &quot;&lt;64-hex&gt;&quot;, &quot;position&quot;: &quot;left&quot;|&quot;right&quot; } indicating whether the sibling is to the left or right of the current node.</para>
<para>Leaf identity is (adapter_id, version) — both fields are required to unambiguously locate a leaf when multiple versions of the same adapter appear in one batch. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
